    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Edward Suess classified the Earth's interior into three distinct layers based on chemical composition: SIAL, SIMA, and NIFE.",
        "SIAL consists predominantly of Silica and Aluminium, forming the upper layer of the continental crust with an average density of 2.7 g/cm³.",
        "SIMA is composed of Silica and Magnesium, forming the oceanic floor and underlying continental layer with a density ranging from 2.9 to 4.7 g/cm³.",
        "NIFE forms the core of the Earth, dominated by Nickel and Iron (Ferrum), exhibiting extremely high density (11–13 g/cm³) and rigid magnetic properties."
      ],
